{
  "rationale": "The plant automata model the robot's perception (obstacle sensors) and motion capabilities (discrete actions). The specifications bind sensor outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforce conservative recovery, and prevent unsafe or oscillatory behaviors. Recovery actions are brief and forward progress is resumed as soon as possible. full_rotate and move_backward are only used in last-resort or dedicated recovery states.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate perception and motion into distinct plant automata for clarity and modularity.",
    "Specifications bind sensor outcomes to actions, enforce safe recovery, and prevent repeated or unsafe actions (e.g., no repeated full_rotate, no chaining move_backward, no oscillatory turns)."
  ],
